  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[This question is adapted from Exercise 5, p. 26, in Section 6 of Bokhove, C., Thoma, A., Gammack, D., Yu, L. H. S., Roberts, S. and Downey, F., Thinking about Proof, 1st edition, University of Southampton, 2022: it asks for the least value of sin x cos x + 1, and for the smallest constant c that keeps a sin x cos x + c from being negative.]]></text></questiondescription>
